      "description": "Watch Portland Timbers vs Real Salt Lake highlights and goals from Major League Soccer on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 26, 2026. The atmosphere was electric as Portland Timbers and Real Salt Lake faced off in a high-stakes MLS clash. Fans at the stadium expected a battle of tactics and grit, but few could have predicted the series of events that would unfold under the lights. Early Dominance and a Costly Red Card On July 26, 2026, the match began with both sides displaying high intensity from the opening whistle. Real Salt Lake wasted no time in making their mark, silencing the home crowd in the 18th minute when Juan Sanabria found the back of the net, thanks to a well-placed assist from Morgan Guilavogui . However, the momentum shifted drastically just after the half-hour mark. Guilavogui , who had been instrumental in the opening goal, was shown a straight red card in the 31st minute. His dismissal followed heavy protests from his teammates, leaving the visitors to play over an hour with only ten men. Mora Inspires the Second Half Comeback Capitalizing on their numerical advantage, Portland Timbers came out for the second half with renewed attacking intent. Their persistence paid off in the 56th minute when Ariel Lassiter set up Felipe Mora for the equalizer, igniting the home support. The pressure didn't stop there. In the 67th minute, Kristoffer Velde provided the service for Felipe Mora to strike again, scoring his second goal of the night and completing the turnaround. The clinical finishing of the forward turned the tide of a match that had initially looked difficult for the hosts. Defensive Resilience in the Final Stages In an attempt to salvage a point, Real Salt Lake introduced fresh legs like Alexandros Katranis and Joao Ortiz late in the game. Portland responded by fortifying their defense, bringing on Jose Caicedo and Alexander Aravena to see out the victory. Despite eight minutes of stoppage time and a flurry of tactical substitutions from both managers, Portland Timbers maintained their discipline to secure the win, successfully navigating a chaotic encounter defined by a pivotal red card and a brilliant individual performance."
